<title>HONG KONG: HK observatory reports quake of 5.6 in Philippines.</title>
<headline>HK observatory reports quake of 5.6 in Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>An intense earthquake estimated at 5.6 on the Richter scale was recorded 1,100 km (688 miles) south-southeast of the Philippine capital Manila on Friday, the Royal Hong Kong Observatory said.</p>
<p>The quake was recorded at 12.20 p.m. (1620 GMT Thursday).</p>
<p>The epicentre was initially determined to be off the southern coast of the Philippines about 1,100 km south-southeast of Manila, the observatory said.</p>
